 "silent_error": "rsem-calculate-expression --alignments requires all alignments of a read to be adjacent in the file (its usage text: 'RSEM requires all alignments of the same read group together'); a coordinate-sorted BAM (the file here was written by 'samtools sort', header SO:coordinate) breaks that. RSEM does not check it: alignments that are not adjacent are treated as separate reads, so a read that aligns to both isoforms (the first 400 nt are shared) becomes two independent reads. The log shows 'N = 143' reads instead of 115 and the expected counts are inflated and wrongly split (ENST00000610001 48.00 and ENST00000610002 40.00 instead of 37.21 and 22.79; the total is 143 instead of 115). Nothing is reported, exit 0, and the results file is well formed. The clean run name-sorts the BAM first so that alignments of one read are adjacent.",
